{
  "all_converged": true,
  "conclusion": "Instance area is um^2 and perim is um (candidate C1). C3 (um^2 x 1e12 / um x 1e6, the old design/README.md reading) is refuted by a factor of 1e12 on BOTH the capacitance path and the current path. C2 (m^2 / m, the cards literal ; Units: comments) is numerically indistinguishable from C1 at the same instance values but is disposed of on physical consistency: under C2 the measured capacitance density is 1e12 times below the cards own stated F/m^2 figure, and 1 instance unit would be 1 m^2 of diode. The cards pre-scale cj (*1e-12, F/m^2 -> F/um^2), cjsw (*1e-6, F/m -> F/um) and ik (/1e-12, A/m^2 -> A/um^2) to match the um-based instance convention; js, jsw and rs carry NO such factor and ngspice applies them raw per instance unit (effective A/um^2, A/um, ohm*um^2), so their ; Units: ... meter ... comments describe pre-conversion source units, not the units the instance numbers are in. The design netlists area=2e14 perim=6e7 therefore instantiate a 2e14 um^2 = 200 m^2 diode.",
  "corner": "tt",
  "kind": "probe",
  "note": "Settles a unit convention, which is corner- and temperature-independent; tt / 27 C is the repo convention and the .temp 30 companion deck (the cards own tref) only closes the residual measured/card ratio of the current path as a temperature artifact. GMIN is left at the ngspice default 1e-12 S: the primary current-path point is 0.6 V forward, well above the floor, and the recorded 0.2 / 0.3 / 0.4 V rows are the measured demonstration of why a low-bias operating point cannot settle this. The perim= / pj= alias is asserted from the devices own readback, not assumed. No device is resized and no ESD rating is stated anywhere; the a=2e14 / p=6e7 anchors record what the design netlists placeholder MEANS, not a sizing proposal (G1, decision 0004). Nothing under sim/diode-probe/ was touched (append-only).",
  "pdk_revision": "f6eeac7dad085ffcc829ccfd721f7b4ce39edcf7",
  "pdk_variant": "sky130A",
  "probe": "diode instance area/perim unit-convention probe (sky130_fd_pr__diode_pd2nw_05v5, sky130_fd_pr__diode_pw2nd_05v5), issue #107",
